Package: alot
Title: A Rust Backend for Building and Rendering 'ggplot2' Plots
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Ruarai", "Tobin", email = "ruarai.tobin@unimelb.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Re-implements the 'ggplot2' build step (ggplot_build()) and
    rendering to SVG/PNG, with performance-critical work in Rust. Components
    without a Rust implementation fall back to 'ggplot2' itself, so output is
    identical to 'ggplot2'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.4)
Imports:
    cli,
    grDevices,
    ggplot2 (>= 4.0.0),
    ggplot2 (< 4.1.0),
    grid,
    ragg (>= 1.5.0),
    ragg (< 1.6.0),
    labeling,
    scales,
    systemfonts (>= 1.2.0),
    rlang,
    S7,
    utils,
    vctrs
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.78.0
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
